## Third-party components

Jarvis itself is MIT. It depends on other people's work, which keeps its own
licence:

| Component | Licence | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| OpenAI Python SDK, `websockets`, `numpy`, `sounddevice`, `pillow`, `pywebview` | MIT / BSD | permissive, no obligations beyond attribution |
| `pystray` | LGPL-3.0 | used unmodified as a library |
| `sherpa-onnx` | Apache-2.0 | local wake-word engine |
| Wake-word model (`sherpa-onnx-kws-zipformer-gigaspeech-3.3M`) | Apache-2.0 declared | **the tarball ships no LICENSE file, and the GigaSpeech audio corpus carries non-commercial research terms** — read the model's own terms before any commercial redistribution of that model |
| OpenAI API | commercial terms | you bring your own key and pay OpenAI directly |

The **vendored OpenAI documentation** used to verify the API contract is NOT
redistributed in this repository; see `docs/OPENAI-API-NOTES.md` for what was
checked and links to the source pages.
